WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.920
Good morning, Hank. It's Wednesday.

00:00:00.920 --> 00:00:05.620
We were gonna have a video from the dftba.com
warehouse today, but I thought I’d make one instead.

00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:09.220
So it appears that more Americans voted for
Hillary Clinton than Donald Trump in the U.S.

00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:13.400
presidential race, but the presidential race
is decided by electoral college votes, and

00:00:13.401 --> 00:00:16.759
Donald Trump won most of them, so he is the
President-Elect.

00:00:16.759 --> 00:00:20.530
Most, although certainly not all, of the people
watching this video wanted Hillary Clinton

00:00:20.530 --> 00:00:25.230
to become President (I know I did), and for
many of us, the results of the election are devastating.

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:28.640
I think part of what makes it so hard for
some people is that Donald Trump has often

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:33.770
attacked not what his opponents believe, but
who they are: their race, their gender, their

00:00:33.770 --> 00:00:35.090
religion, and more.

00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:40.500
And it is painful and scary to be called dangerous
or less than by a man who becomes President-Elect

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:45.040
of the United States, and I don’t want to
minimize that fear or trauma because I believe

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:47.040
that it is real and important.

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:48.400
I also want to say that I’m sorry.

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:52.680
I’m sorry that we have let our political
discourse become so hateful, and I’m sorry

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:56.960
that we’ve let our echo chambers become
so sealed off that it is as unfathomable to

00:00:56.960 --> 00:01:01.460
me why someone would support Donald Trump
for President as it is to many Trump supporters

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:03.300
why I would support Hillary Clinton.

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:06.590
I spoke with hundreds of undecided voters
in the days before the election, and what

00:01:06.590 --> 00:01:09.729
struck me most was how different our information
was.

00:01:09.729 --> 00:01:13.929
In many cases, we had the same concerns: the
environment, or health care, or tax policy,

00:01:13.929 --> 00:01:17.340
but we were working with completely different
data sets.

00:01:17.350 --> 00:01:19.780
Our community, by the way, is also an echo
chamber.

00:01:19.789 --> 00:01:23.700
Just 4% of the nerdfighters who filled out
the census this year said they would vote

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:24.520
for Donald Trump.

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:28.119
But I don’t know how to make our community
more inclusive without opening it up to cruelty

00:01:28.119 --> 00:01:29.059
and hatred.

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:33.040
We have to get better at listening to each
other and challenging each other constructively

00:01:33.049 --> 00:01:37.479
and generously, but I worry that the very
architecture of the social internet might

00:01:37.479 --> 00:01:38.779
make that impossible.

00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:43.799
Honestly, I feel lost, and I’m looking to
you for guidance and clarity, as I have for

00:01:43.799 --> 00:01:45.119
almost a decade now.

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:46.560
But the world doesn’t end today.

00:01:46.570 --> 00:01:50.310
As Saladin Ahmed wrote last night, “It’s
our job to fight those in power and stick

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:51.430
up for the powerless.

00:01:51.430 --> 00:01:53.770
That stays the same no matter who’s President.”

00:01:53.770 --> 00:01:57.950
As Lin Manuel Miranda wrote, “I love this
country, and there’s more work to do than ever."

00:01:57.950 --> 00:02:01.410
And as Kamala Harris said, “This is a time
to fight for who we are.”

00:02:01.410 --> 00:02:03.620
I think this will be a tough time in U.S.
history.

00:02:03.630 --> 00:02:05.730
I hope it won’t be, but I think it will
be.

00:02:05.730 --> 00:02:10.140
But I also think our nation is and always
must be bigger than any of its leaders, and

00:02:10.149 --> 00:02:14.009
that our leaders are and always must be answerable
to the people.

00:02:14.009 --> 00:02:18.240
So it’s always our job to stand together
and make sure the government does its job.

00:02:18.250 --> 00:02:22.370
That it affords equal protection under the
law to all citizens, that the rights of all

00:02:22.370 --> 00:02:27.050
are protected, and that our government’s
policies are fiscally sound and carefully considered.

00:02:27.050 --> 00:02:31.210
Change doesn’t only happen on election night,
and it doesn’t only happen in the Oval Office,

00:02:31.210 --> 00:02:35.939
and it is up to us to find the places where
our skills and talents meet the needs of our

00:02:35.939 --> 00:02:40.659
community and the world, and to do the hard
work to make life better for all.

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:42.980
And on that front, I am hopeful.

00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:47.080
So ten days ago, my nephew Orin was born,
and bringing that baby into the world was

00:02:47.090 --> 00:02:49.590
an act of hope on the part of his parents.

00:02:49.590 --> 00:02:53.830
I am glad for their hope, and I am heartened
by it, and I do not believe it was misguided.

00:02:53.830 --> 00:02:57.680
That child was born into an America that is
better than the one his grandparents were

00:02:57.680 --> 00:03:02.319
born into, and it was made better by people
whose hope, from restaurant counters in Alabama

00:03:02.319 --> 00:03:07.909
to the beaches of Normandy help them to stand
together and hold the line in circumstances

00:03:07.909 --> 00:03:12.250
vastly darker than anything I pray most of
us will ever see.

00:03:12.250 --> 00:03:14.260
I don’t think hope is idealistic or silly.

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:16.569
I think it’s the founding emotion of our
species.

00:03:16.569 --> 00:03:20.900
And it’s not naive to hope that we can bend
the arc of American history toward justice,

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:25.160
because we’ve seen our ancestors do that
in the face of unimaginable difficulty.

00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:29.500
As the great American poet of the human heart
wrote, “Hope is the thing with feathers

00:03:29.510 --> 00:03:36.930
that perches in the soul and sings the tune
without the words and never stops at all.”

00:03:36.930 --> 00:03:38.250
Take care of yourself.

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:40.180
And take care of each other.

